  "question": {
    "text": "0.5 g of an organic compound on combustion gave 1.46 g of $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ and 0.9 g of $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}$. The percentage of carbon in the compound is _______. (Nearest integer) [Given : Molar mass (in $\\mathrm{g} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$) $\\mathrm{C}: 12, \\mathrm{H}: 1$, O: 16]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "80",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Organic $\\rightarrow \\mathrm{CO}_2$<br />Compound<br />Applying POAC on ' C '<br />(mole) of ' C ' in compound $=\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{CO}_2} \\times 1$<br />So mass of ' C ' in compound<br />$=\\frac{1.46}{44} \\times 12$<br />So, $\\%$ of ' C ' in compound $=\\frac{1.46}{44} \\times \\frac{12}{0.5} \\times 100$<br />$=79.63$",
    "image": null
  },
